From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: re5osx <re5osx@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasm2c: opt-in caller instance for call_indirect

WASM_RT_NONCONFORMING_CALLER_INSTANCE: call_indirect passes the calling
function's instance, not the one stored in the table entry. A program
that runs one instance of the same module per thread (wasm threads over a
shared memory) can then give every instance one shared table instead of a
copy each; the copies differ only in the instance their entries hold. For
a module with ~90k table entries this is ~2.9 MB per thread.
---
 src/template/wasm2c.declarations.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/template/wasm2c.declarations.c b/src/template/wasm2c.declarations.c
--- a/src/template/wasm2c.declarations.c
+++ b/src/template/wasm2c.declarations.c
@@ -126,7 +126,17 @@
   (LIKELY((x) < table.size && ft == table.data[x].func_type) || \
    func_types_eq_slowpath(&(table), ft, x))
 
+// WASM_RT_NONCONFORMING_CALLER_INSTANCE: call_indirect passes the calling
+// function's instance instead of the one the table entry holds, so that the
+// instances of one module (one per thread) can share a single table. Only for
+// trusted modules whose tables hold nothing but their own functions, and host
+// functions that take the caller's instance.
+#if WASM_RT_NONCONFORMING_CALLER_INSTANCE
+#define DO_CALL_INDIRECT(table, t, x, entry_instance, ...) \
+  ((t)table.data[x].func)(instance, ##__VA_ARGS__)
+#else
 #define DO_CALL_INDIRECT(table, t, x, ...) ((t)table.data[x].func)(__VA_ARGS__)
+#endif
 
 // WASM_RT_NONCONFORMING_UNCHECKED_CALL_INDIRECT skips the table bounds and
 // signature checks of call_indirect. Only for trusted modules.
-- 
